// The block pattern (D197, D215, D290): a block kind's cubes drawn as one surface, rounded
// along its outside edges and given relief by its material's maps, so a wall of any shape,
// carved anywhere, is one wall with no seams (crates/terra_build/src/surface.rs); every
// exposed edge dressed by its role in pieces this pattern shares with every material of it,
// each drawn in the material's own bake. A material of it (stone, earth, lime) is a few
// lines naming this pattern and its pack (docs/proposals/construction-002.md).
//
// pattern     Masonry: laid as its cubes' surface (`layout::blocks`)
// bevel       the radius its outside edges are rounded to, in metres
// relief      how far its material stands out, from the deepest joint to the proudest face
// timber      its lintels' and sills' timber, where a role takes timber (D200)
// textures    the texture sets its pieces wear unless a pack says otherwise: Dressed for its
//             dressed stone, Log and LogEnd for timber; a pack adds its Masonry (the walls
//             and footings) and Floor (floors and walls' tops)
// dress       the pieces every block material shares (tools/kits/pieces.py, art/kits/block):
//             a coping on every top, a plinth along every foot stepping with the ground,
//             quoins up every outside corner, a lintel, sill and jamb stones round every
//             opening, a cap under a thinner wall standing on it, a fascia under an overhang,
//             a tread on every step and a border round a floor; posts as pillars 36 cm square
// meets       heavier than timber (weight 3), so it runs through a joint with it, quoined up
//             its end, and caps its top where timber stands on it (D232)
// colours     light: the colour of the dust it throws up as it comes down; a pack's own
// toughness  how much damage a cube takes before it is destroyed (D193, D305); half its
//             cost to repair from nothing; breaking into chunks (`fragments::Breaks`)
// damage      how it breaks as it loses its health (D305): its walls, floors and dressed
//             stone at their joints (the lowest share of its height map), the mortar first,
//             then the stones' edges, then whole stones, leaving holes so deep (a wall's
//             deeper than a stone is thick, dark at their back)
(
    pattern: Masonry,
    toughness: (health: 600, breaks: Chunks),
    damage: {
        Masonry: Joints(share: 0.22, depth: 0.16),
        Floor: Joints(share: 0.2, depth: 0.04),
        Dressed: Joints(share: 0.12, depth: 0.04),
    },
    bevel: 0.04,
    relief: 0.05,
    timber: (
        profile: Hewn,
        notch: Flush,
        relief: 0.0,
        tint: (0.9, 0.84, 0.76),
        end_tint: (0.86, 0.82, 0.78),
    ),
    textures: {
        Dressed: (path: "materials/rock_boulder_dry", metres: (0.9, 0.9)),
        Log: (path: "materials/rough_wood", metres: (0.5, 0.5)),
        LogEnd: (path: "materials/log_end", metres: (1.0, 1.0)),
    },
    dress: (
        pieces: Some("data/kits/pieces/block.ron"),
        roles: {
            Crest: Profile(name: "coping"),
            Nose: Profile(name: "nose"),
            Sill: Profile(name: "sill", extend: 0.06),
            Head: Profile(name: "lintel", extend: 0.2, joints: false),
            Soffit: Profile(name: "fascia"),
            Foot: Profile(name: "plinth"),
            Meet: Profile(name: "cap"),
            Border: Profile(name: "border"),
            Arris: Corners(set: "quoin"),
            Jamb: Corners(set: "jamb"),
            Post: Pillar(width: 0.36),
        },
    ),
    meets: Some((weight: 3, end: None, carries: Cap)),
    colours: (
        light: (0.62, 0.6, 0.56),
    ),
)
